From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Subject: net: stmmac: match the compatible through the fwnode, not the of_node

stmmac_probe_config_dt() decides which DWMAC core it is talking to by
testing the "compatible" strings with of_device_is_compatible(). That walks
dev->of_node, which is NULL for a device described by ACPI PRP0001, so none
of those tests can ever match and plat->core_type is left at its allocation
default - DWMAC_CORE_MAC100, the first enum value.

The failure is silent rather than loud. stmmac_get_version() returns early
for MAC100 without reading the ID register, so nothing reports a mismatch;
the driver simply proceeds as a 20-year-old MAC100 on a DWMAC 3.70a:

  meson8b-dwmac PRP0001:03:        DWMAC100
  meson8b-dwmac PRP0001:03: No HW DMA feature register supported
  meson8b-dwmac PRP0001:03: device MAC address 00:00:00:00:04:00
  meson8b-dwmac PRP0001:03: error -EIO: Cannot register the MDIO bus
  meson8b-dwmac PRP0001:03: probe with driver meson8b-dwmac failed with error -5

The MAC is healthy throughout - on a VIM3 GMAC_VERSION reads 0x00001137 and
the address registers hold the address the firmware programmed. Only the
core selection is wrong, and everything downstream follows from it.

device_is_compatible() answers from the fwnode, so it resolves DeviceTree
and ACPI alike, and is a straight substitution for the DeviceTree path.
of_device_compatible_match() has no fwnode counterpart, so match the
NULL-terminated list with a small local helper.

The remaining of_device_is_compatible() call, in stmmac_of_get_mdio(),
walks DeviceTree child nodes and is deliberately left alone.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_platform.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_platform.c
index 6128ed1bd521..621c6ab055a7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_platform.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_platform.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_net.h>
 #include <linux/of_mdio.h>
+#include <linux/property.h>
 
 #include "stmmac.h"
 #include "stmmac_platform.h"
@@ -402,6 +403,22 @@ static const char * const stmmac_gmac4_compats[] = {
 	NULL
 };
 
+/* Match the device's "compatible" against a NULL-terminated list.
+ *
+ * Unlike of_device_compatible_match() this resolves both DeviceTree and ACPI
+ * devices: an ACPI device described with PRP0001 carries its "compatible"
+ * strings in _DSD, and has no dev->of_node for the of_*() helpers to walk.
+ */
+static bool stmmac_device_compatible_match(struct device *dev,
+					   const char *const *compats)
+{
+	while (*compats)
+		if (device_is_compatible(dev, *compats++))
+			return true;
+
+	return false;
+}
